# Augment Guidelines for rippled Project

## Build System

### Local Builds (Default)

This project uses local compilation with ccache for faster incremental builds.

#### Build Commands

Standard build with logging (recommended):
```bash
cd .build && ninja -j4 2>&1 | tee build.log
```

Build with output redirected to file only (quieter):
```bash
cd .build && ninja -j4 > build.log 2>&1
```

#### Parallelism Settings

- **Local machine has 4 CPU cores**
- Recommended: `ninja -j4` (one job per core)
- For memory-constrained builds: `ninja -j2`

#### Build Logging

Always capture build output to log files for debugging:
- `2>&1 | tee build.log` - Shows output and saves to file
- `> build.log 2>&1` - Redirects all output to file (quieter)
- Log files are created in the `.build/` directory

#### Clean Build

```bash
cd .build
ninja -t clean
ninja -j4 2>&1 | tee build.log
```

#### ccache Integration

ccache is configured for faster incremental builds:
- Max size: 10 GB
- Compiler check: content
- Hash dir: false

Check ccache statistics:
```bash
ccache -s
```

Clear ccache if needed:
```bash
ccache -C
```

### CMake Configuration

The project uses CMake with Ninja generator. To reconfigure:

```bash
cd .build
cmake /home/edesouza/Projects/rippled -G Ninja \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
    -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/usr/bin/gcc-13 \
    -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/usr/bin/g++-13 \
    -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache \
    -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache \
    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=/home/edesouza/Projects/rippled/.build/build/generators/conan_toolchain.cmake
```

To build xrpld binary (not just library), add `-Dxrpld=ON`.

### Distributed Compilation with distcc-pump (Optional/Alternative)

For faster builds when remote build servers are available, distcc-pump can be used.
**Note**: This is optional and not the default build method.

#### Environment Setup for distcc

```bash
# Disable any existing distcc settings first
unset DISTCC_HOSTS
unset CCACHE_PREFIX

# Set the distcc hosts (4 remote servers with 4 jobs each)
export DISTCC_HOSTS="10.100.1.17,cpp,lzo/4 10.100.1.18,cpp,lzo/4 10.100.1.19,cpp,lzo/4 10.100.1.20,cpp,lzo/4"
```

#### Building with distcc-pump

```bash
cd .build && distcc-pump ninja -j20 2>&1 | tee build.log
```

**Important**: Use `distcc-pump` (not plain `distcc`) because:
- Pump mode distributes preprocessing to remote hosts
- This avoids Intel AMX intrinsics header incompatibilities
- Plain distcc preprocesses locally which can cause build failures

#### Troubleshooting distcc

1. Clear backoff files: `rm -rf ~/.distcc/lock/backoff*`
2. Check remote hosts: `nc -zv 10.100.1.17 3632`
3. Verify GCC version matches local (13.3.0): `g++-13 --version`
4. Ensure include_server symlink exists at `/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/include_server`

## Code Style

- Run `pre-commit run clang-format --files <files>` before committing
- The project uses C++20 standard

## Testing

